WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.879
In this next section, we're going

2
00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:06.769
to create the main level sequence for our exercise.

3
00:00:06.769 --> 00:00:10.169
To do that, we are going to add the level sequence

4
00:00:10.169 --> 00:00:11.609
either one of two options.

5
00:00:11.609 --> 00:00:14.009
We can do it within our content browser,

6
00:00:14.009 --> 00:00:16.230
or we can do it from our menu.

7
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.969
Let's jump over to the project real fast,

8
00:00:17.969 --> 00:00:21.170
and I'll show you where both those options exist.

9
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:24.250
So we can add a sequence from the main toolbar

10
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.050
and do add level sequence.

11
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.489
Or if you prefer to create your sequence

12
00:00:29.489 --> 00:00:32.649
in a specific folder, we can open up our content browser.

13
00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:35.850
And in this case, I'm going to go to our courses, sequence

14
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.009
105.

15
00:00:37.009 --> 00:00:41.450
And I've got this map here, this folder, sequence example.

16
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.450
You can do that too by right clicking and adding a folder.

17
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.729
Name it whatever you'd like.

18
00:00:45.729 --> 00:00:48.810
And inside of there, we can right click cinematics

19
00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.189
and add a level sequence.

20
00:00:50.189 --> 00:00:51.530
So we'll go ahead and do that.

21
00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:55.850
And we'll just call this SCQ for sequence underscore 105.

22
00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:00.100
And then I'll just type in example.

23
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.619
Now before we dive into creating the camera and character

24
00:01:02.619 --> 00:01:04.980
animations in our sequence, let's

25
00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.420
cover the basics of working with level sequences

26
00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.019
and how and where they should be placed.

27
00:01:10.019 --> 00:01:11.859
Sequences are independent actors

28
00:01:11.859 --> 00:01:14.500
that often reference content from within our levels,

29
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.819
but they can function independently of a level.

30
00:01:17.819 --> 00:01:20.900
It's a common practice to add the sequence actor to a level,

31
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:24.260
since the sequence often references level actors.

32
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.980
As a best practice recommendation,

33
00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:29.439
you can either, one, name the sequence after the level,

34
00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:31.879
or place it directly in it.

35
00:01:31.879 --> 00:01:34.359
Either option provides clarity on which level

36
00:01:34.359 --> 00:01:37.319
the sequence is associated with, but for our exercise,

37
00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:39.719
we'll add the sequence actor into the level.

38
00:01:39.719 --> 00:01:42.189
So let's jump back to the project real fast,

39
00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:43.989
and I'll show you how to do that.

40
00:01:43.989 --> 00:01:46.829
So once our sequence is created, all we need to do

41
00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:49.969
is just drag that actor into the world.

42
00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:52.370
I'll switch on game mode, and you can see now

43
00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.689
we have that sequence actor available,

44
00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:56.530
so we know that it's going to be referencing

45
00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.450
the content within our level.
